We first performed a GWA analysis on 388 DH lines using bi-allelic SNPs. The dataset was pruned with PLINK (Purcell et al. 2007) to remove redundant markers (r2 > 0.99 within a 300 kb window). Given the high marker density, SNPs that showed r2 < 0.8 with all other markers within 10 Mb distance were considered erroneous and excluded. This resulted in a final set of 359,141 SNPs. Association analyses were conducted on the adjusted entry means from individual trials and means across trials using vcf2gwas (Vogt et al. 2022), which implements a mixed linear model of GEMMA (Zhou and Stephens 2012):2\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
