We studied potential pleiotropy of QTL for proxy traits and grain yield using bivariate multi-trait models. Each model included adjusted means of grain yield estimated across testcross trials together with adjusted means of one proxy trait estimated across line per se trials. The bivariate multi-trait model of Korte et al. (2012) was implemented using the R package StatgenQTLxT (https://github.com/Biometris/statgenQTLxT). Extending the model in Eq. (2) \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
